S="Advent: The King Is Coming"
D("2026-11-30",S,"The Youngest Son","a 3rd–5th grader","1 Samuel 16:7",[(7,"But the LORD said to Samuel, “Do not look on his appearance or on the height of his stature, because I have rejected him. For the LORD sees not as man sees: man looks on the outward appearance, but the LORD looks on the heart.”")],
"David is anointed",[
"Israel’s first king, Saul, stopped listening to God. So God sent Samuel, now an old prophet, to Bethlehem. “Go to the house of a man named Jesse. I have chosen one of his sons to be the next king.” Samuel took a horn of oil to anoint the new king.",
"Jesse brought out his oldest son, Eliab, who was tall and handsome. Samuel thought, “Surely this is the one!” But God said, “Don’t look at how tall he is. People look at the outside, but the Lord looks at the heart.” Seven sons walked by, and God said no to each one. “Are these all your sons?” Samuel asked.",
"“Well, there’s still the youngest, David. He’s out watching the sheep.” They sent for him. When the shepherd boy walked in, God said, “This is the one. Anoint him.” Samuel poured the oil on David’s head, and the Spirit of the Lord came on David from that day on. Bethlehem’s youngest shepherd would be king."],
"God sees the heart",["God chose the one nobody expected. Years later, another King would be born in Bethlehem, in a stable, and many would overlook Him too. “Christ” means “Anointed One.” Jesus is the King God chose to save us."],
["Which town did Samuel go to? Where was David when they sent for him?","What does God look at instead of how people look?","David was anointed with oil; “Christ” means “Anointed One.” How does David’s story point to Jesus?"],
"Lord God, thank You that You look at the heart. Thank You for choosing David, and for sending Jesus, the Anointed King, from David’s family.","Help us see others the way You see them.",
"God chose David, the youngest shepherd, to be king. God looks at the heart!",
["Samuel went to the town of [Bethlehem].","David’s father was named [Jesse].","David was out watching the [sheep].","The Lord looks at the [heart].","Samuel poured [oil] on David’s head."],
["DAVID","JESSE","OIL","HEART","KING","SHEPHERD"],[("Did God choose the tallest son?",["Yes","No"],1),("What does God look at?",["The heart","Clothes"],0)],
"Draw Samuel pouring oil on David’s head.",("1 Samuel 16:7","“The LORD looks on the heart.”"),
scene(hills(),person(200,beard=True,arms="up",hair="wrap"),person(310,beard=False,arms="open",hair="curly",s=.75),sheep(460),sheep(560,.8),'<path d="M226,118 q16,-8 26,8 l-4,6 q-10,-8 -20,-4 Z"/>',label="Coloring picture: Samuel anointing young David"))

D("2026-12-01",S,"David and Goliath","an older kid","1 Samuel 17:45",[(45,"Then David said to the Philistine, “You come to me with a sword and with a spear and with a javelin, but I come to you in the name of the LORD of hosts, the God of the armies of Israel, whom you have defied.")],
"The giant",[
"The Philistine army had a champion named Goliath, a giant over nine feet tall with heavy bronze armor and a spear as thick as a tree branch. Every day he shouted at Israel’s army: “Send someone to fight me!” And every day, King Saul and all his soldiers were terrified.",
"Young David came to bring food to his brothers and heard Goliath mocking God. “Who is this man to defy the armies of the living God?” David told Saul, “I’ll fight him. God saved me from a lion and a bear when I protected my sheep. He’ll save me from this giant.” Saul offered his armor, but it was too big. David took only his shepherd’s staff, his sling, and five smooth stones.",
"Goliath laughed. But David said, “You come with a sword and spear, but I come in the name of the Lord.” David ran toward the giant, swung his sling, and the stone hit Goliath right in the forehead. The giant fell face down. Israel won, because the battle belonged to the Lord."],
"The battle is the Lord’s",["David didn’t win because he was big or strong. He trusted God. Jesus, the Son of David, faced a much bigger enemy, sin, death, and the devil, and He won that battle for us on the cross."],
["What did David bring to fight Goliath? How many stones did he pick?","Why wasn’t David afraid when everyone else was?","What “giants” do people face today? How did Jesus, the Son of David, defeat the biggest giant of all?"],
"Lord of hosts, thank You for giving David courage and victory. Thank You for Jesus, who defeated sin, death, and the devil for us.","When we face giants, help us trust that the battle is Yours.",
"Young David fought the giant Goliath with a sling and a stone, in the name of the Lord!",
["The giant’s name was [Goliath].","David picked up five smooth [stones].","He used a [sling].","David came in the name of the [Lord].","The stone hit Goliath’s [forehead]."],
["GOLIATH","SLING","STONES","GIANT","DAVID","BATTLE"],[("Did David wear Saul’s armor?",["Yes","No"],1),("Who won the battle for David?",["The Lord","David’s muscles"],0)],
"Draw David with his sling facing the giant.",("1 Samuel 17:45","“I come to you in the name of the LORD of hosts.”"),
scene(hills(),giant(430),person(170,beard=False,arms="up",hair="curly",s=.75),sling(176,138),stones(220,3),label="Coloring picture: young David with a sling facing the giant Goliath"))

D("2026-12-02",S,"The Lord Is My Shepherd","a K–2nd grader, with help","Psalm 23:1–3",[(1,"The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want."),(2,"He makes me lie down in green pastures. He leads me beside still waters."),(3,"He restores my soul. He leads me in paths of righteousness for his name’s sake.")],
"David’s song",[
"Before David was king, he was a shepherd. He knew exactly what sheep need. They need green grass to eat and calm water to drink, because sheep are scared of rushing water. They need someone to lead them on safe paths and protect them from wolves and bears. Without a shepherd, sheep get lost.",
"David also played the harp and wrote songs to God. One day he thought, “I take care of my sheep… and God takes care of me like that!” So he wrote the most famous psalm of all: “The Lord is my shepherd; I shall not want.”",
"In the psalm, the Shepherd feeds us, leads us, restores us when we’re worn out, and stays with us even in the darkest valley. He even prepares a table for us and fills our cup to overflowing. And David ends with a promise: “I shall dwell in the house of the Lord forever.”"],
"The Good Shepherd",["Jesus said, “I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep.” David protected his sheep from lions. Jesus gave His life for His sheep. That means you."],
["What did David take care of? What did he play?","What does a good shepherd do for his sheep?","Jesus calls Himself the Good Shepherd (John 10:11). What does He do that even David couldn’t?"],
"Lord Jesus, You are our Good Shepherd. Thank You for feeding us, leading us, and laying down Your life for us.","Lead us in Your paths and keep us close to You.",
"David wrote, “The Lord is my shepherd.” Jesus is our Good Shepherd who takes care of us!",
["David was a [shepherd].","He played the [harp].","The Lord is my [shepherd].","He leads me beside still [waters].","Jesus is the [Good] Shepherd."],
["SHEPHERD","SHEEP","PSALM","HARP","WATERS","PASTURE"],[("Who is our Good Shepherd?",["Jesus","A farmer"],0),("Does the Shepherd leave us in the dark valley?",["Yes","No"],1)],
"Draw the Good Shepherd with His sheep by still waters.",("Psalm 23:1","“The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want.”"),
scene(hills(),'<path d="M400,280 q60,-14 120,0 q60,14 116,0" fill="none"/>'+waves(288,400,636),person(200,beard=True,arms="open",hair="short"),lamb(110),sheep(310),sheep(380,.8),label="Coloring picture: the Good Shepherd with sheep by still waters"))

D("2026-12-03",S,"Unto Us a Child Is Born","an older kid","Isaiah 9:6",[(6,"For to us a child is born, to us a son is given; and the government shall be upon his shoulder, and his name shall be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.")],
"Isaiah’s promise",[
"About 700 years before Jesus was born, God gave a prophet named Isaiah some amazing messages. Isaiah lived in a dark time. Enemies were attacking, kings were making bad choices, and people had turned away from God. Many people felt like they were walking in darkness.",
"But God gave Isaiah a promise of light: a child would be born, a son would be given. And this child would be no ordinary baby. He would be a King whose kingdom would grow forever. Isaiah listed His names, and each one tells us something about Him.",
"Wonderful Counselor: He knows exactly what we need. Mighty God: this baby would be God Himself! Everlasting Father: He would care for His people forever. Prince of Peace: He would make peace between God and people. The people waited seven hundred years. Then, one night in Bethlehem, the child was born."],
"His names",["Isaiah 9:6 is one of the clearest promises of Jesus in the whole Old Testament. A baby who is also Mighty God: that’s the wonder of Christmas. God became a child for us. Many people hear these words every Christmas in Handel’s “Messiah.”"],
["How long before Jesus did Isaiah live? Can you remember the four names?","Which of Jesus’ four names is your favorite? Why?","How can a baby be “Mighty God”? Why did God need to become a human to save us?"],
"Lord Jesus, You are Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, and Prince of Peace. Thank You for being born for us.","Be our counselor, our strength, and our peace.",
"Isaiah promised, “To us a child is born!” His names are Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace!",
["The prophet’s name was [Isaiah].","To us a [child] is born.","He is Wonderful [Counselor].","He is [Mighty] God.","He is the Prince of [Peace]."],
["ISAIAH","CHILD","COUNSELOR","MIGHTY","PEACE","PRINCE"],[("Was Isaiah’s promise about Jesus?",["Yes","No"],0),("Is the baby Jesus also God?",["Yes","No"],0)],
"Write Jesus’ four names in fancy letters and decorate them.",("Isaiah 9:6","“For to us a child is born, to us a son is given.”"),
scene(bigstar(320,56),person(150,beard=True,arms="up",hair="wrap"),scroll(320,240),manger(500),label="Coloring picture: the prophet Isaiah with a scroll and a manger under a star"))

D("2026-12-04",S,"Little Bethlehem","a 3rd–5th grader","Micah 5:2",[(2,"But you, O Bethlehem Ephrathah, who are too little to be among the clans of Judah, from you shall come forth for me one who is to be ruler in Israel, whose coming forth is from of old, from ancient days.")],
"Micah’s promise",[
"Around the same time as Isaiah, God sent another prophet named Micah. Micah warned the people about their sins: leaders who cheated the poor and people who said they loved God but didn’t act like it. He told them God wants us “to do justice, and to love kindness, and to walk humbly with your God.”",
"But Micah also brought a promise, and it was very specific. The coming King wouldn’t be born in a big important city like Jerusalem. He would be born in Bethlehem, a tiny little town, David’s hometown, too small to be counted among the important places.",
"Seven hundred years later, wise men came looking for a newborn king. King Herod asked the Bible scholars, “Where is the Christ to be born?” And they read Micah’s words: “In Bethlehem.” God had told them exactly where, centuries ahead of time. And His “coming forth is from ancient days,” because Jesus existed before the world began."],
"Small places, big plans",["God loves to use small things: a small town, a shepherd boy, a baby in a manger. Your family might feel small too, but God does big things through little people and little places."],
["Which town did Micah say the King would come from? Whose hometown was it?","Why do you think God picked a tiny town instead of a big city?","How does Micah 5:2 show that Jesus existed before He was born in Bethlehem?"],
"Faithful God, You keep every promise, right down to the town where Jesus would be born. Thank You for using small and humble things.","Help us walk humbly with You and love kindness.",
"Micah promised that the King would be born in little Bethlehem, and that’s exactly where Jesus was born!",
["The prophet’s name was [Micah].","The King would be born in [Bethlehem].","Bethlehem was too [little] to be important.","It was King [David]’s hometown.","God wants us to love [kindness]."],
["MICAH","BETHLEHEM","LITTLE","RULER","PROMISE","KINDNESS"],[("Was Bethlehem a big city?",["Yes","No"],1),("Did God tell the town ahead of time?",["Yes","No"],0)],
"Draw the little town of Bethlehem at night under a star.",("Micah 5:2","“But you, O Bethlehem… from you shall come forth… one who is to be ruler.”"),
scene(bigstar(320,50),stars(12,31,(240,400)),house(130),'<path d="M240,300 V220 h70 v80 M330,300 V200 h80 v100 M250,240 h16 v16 h-16 Z M350,224 h16 v16 h-16 Z"/>',house(520),hills(),label="Coloring picture: the little town of Bethlehem under a star"))

D("2026-12-05",S,"Jonah and the Big Fish","a K–2nd grader, with help","Jonah 2:9",[(9,"But I with the voice of thanksgiving will sacrifice to you; what I have vowed I will pay. Salvation belongs to the LORD!”")],
"Running from God",[
"God told the prophet Jonah, “Go to the big city of Nineveh and tell them to turn away from their evil.” But Jonah didn’t want to go. Nineveh was Israel’s enemy! So Jonah got on a ship going the opposite direction.",
"God sent a terrible storm. The sailors were terrified. Jonah said, “It’s my fault. Throw me into the sea, and it will be calm.” They did, and the sea went still. But God had a plan: He sent a huge fish to swallow Jonah! For three days and three nights Jonah was inside the fish. And there he prayed: “Salvation belongs to the Lord!”",
"God commanded the fish, and it spit Jonah out onto dry land. This time when God said “Go to Nineveh,” Jonah went. He preached, and the whole city, even the king, turned to God and said sorry. And God had mercy on them."],
"The sign of Jonah",["Jesus said that just as Jonah was three days in the fish, He would be three days in the tomb (Matthew 12:40). Jonah came out alive; Jesus rose from the dead. And God’s mercy reaches even enemies like Nineveh, and people like us."],
["Where did God tell Jonah to go? What swallowed Jonah?","Why did Jonah run away? What did he pray inside the fish?","Jesus called His resurrection “the sign of Jonah.” How are their stories alike?"],
"Merciful God, thank You for not giving up on Jonah, or on Nineveh, or on us. Salvation belongs to You!","When we want to run from what You ask, turn us around.",
"Jonah ran from God and got swallowed by a big fish! God gave him another chance.",
["God told Jonah to go to [Nineveh].","Jonah got on a [ship] going the other way.","God sent a big [storm].","A huge [fish] swallowed Jonah.","Jonah prayed, “Salvation belongs to the [Lord]!”"],
["JONAH","FISH","STORM","SHIP","NINEVEH","MERCY"],[("Did Jonah obey God the first time?",["Yes","No"],1),("How long was Jonah in the fish?",["Three days","A week"],0)],
"Draw Jonah inside the big fish.",("Jonah 2:9","“Salvation belongs to the LORD!”"),
scene(waves(110),bigfish(300,210),person(250,beard=True,arms="up",hair="short",s=.45),boat(540,96),cloud(60,40),label="Coloring picture: Jonah inside the big fish"))

D("2026-12-06","St. Nicholas Day","Bishop Nicholas","Mom or Dad","Matthew 6:3–4",[(3,"But when you give to the needy, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing,"),(4,"so that your giving may be in secret. And your Father who sees in secret will reward you.")],
"The real St. Nicholas",[
"Today is St. Nicholas Day, the second Sunday of Advent. Long before Santa Claus, there was a real man named Nicholas. He lived about 300 years after Jesus in a city called Myra, in what is now Turkey. His parents died when he was young and left him money, and Nicholas decided to use it to help people in need. Later he became the bishop, the pastor, of Myra.",
"The most famous story about Nicholas: a poor father had three daughters and no money for them to get married. In those days, that meant a terrible future. So one night, Nicholas secretly tossed a bag of gold through their window. He did it again for the second daughter, and the third. Some say one bag landed in a stocking drying by the fire!",
"Nicholas also stood up for what’s true. When some people taught that Jesus wasn’t truly God, Nicholas defended the faith that Jesus is fully God. He was put in prison for being a Christian, but he never stopped trusting Jesus. Over many years, stories about him grew into the legend of Santa Claus."],
"Giving in secret",["Nicholas gave in secret, just as Jesus taught, because he wasn’t trying to get attention. He gave because Jesus had given him everything. Christmas gifts remind us of the greatest gift: God giving His Son."],
["What did Nicholas toss through the window? How many daughters were there?","Why did Nicholas give in secret? How is the real Nicholas different from Santa?","Nicholas defended the truth that Jesus is God. Why does that matter for Christmas?"],
"Heavenly Father, thank You for Bishop Nicholas and his generous heart. Thank You most of all for giving us Your Son.","Help us give generously and quietly to people in need this Advent.",
"Bishop Nicholas secretly gave gold to a poor family. He gave because Jesus gave him everything!",
["Nicholas lived in the city of [Myra].","He became a [bishop].","He secretly gave bags of [gold].","Jesus said to give in [secret].","Nicholas believed Jesus is truly [God]."],
["NICHOLAS","BISHOP","GOLD","GIVING","SECRET","MYRA"],[("Was Nicholas a real person?",["Yes","No"],0),("Why did Nicholas give?",["Because Jesus gave him everything","To get famous"],0)],
"Draw a secret gift you could give someone this week.",("Matthew 6:4","“Your Father who sees in secret will reward you.”"),
scene(moon(560,56),stars(10,41,(200,640)),house(430),person(180,beard=True,arms="mixed",hair="wrap"),'<path d="M216,118 l8,-20 l8,20 Z"/>',gift(290),'<path d="M380,210 q20,-14 30,0 q-6,16 -18,16 q-14,0 -12,-16 Z"/>',label="Coloring picture: Bishop Nicholas leaving a secret gift at night"))
